1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,294
That ship on Helm's map wasn't there when the game started,

2
00:00:04,744 --> 00:00:07,181
and nothing in your fact sheet can do that.

3
00:00:08,081 --> 00:00:11,154
So today you open the other file, the script.

4
00:00:12,054 --> 00:00:14,363
You'll read it once, from top to bottom,

5
00:00:14,813 --> 00:00:16,897
and then paste three small cards into it.

6
00:00:17,797 --> 00:00:19,914
And you won't write a line of code.

7
00:00:21,714 --> 00:00:24,415
First, a reminder from Lecture 7.

8
00:00:25,315 --> 00:00:28,524
In your fact sheet, a hash is a heading,

9
00:00:28,974 --> 00:00:30,790
and two slashes are a note.

10
00:00:31,690 --> 00:00:34,336
In the script, it's the other way round.

11
00:00:35,236 --> 00:00:36,641
A hash is a note,

12
00:00:37,091 --> 00:00:39,371
and two slashes start a route,

13
00:00:39,821 --> 00:00:42,103
which is a block that runs when something happens.

14
00:00:43,003 --> 00:00:46,868
So a note of your own, in this file, starts with a hash.

15
00:00:48,668 --> 00:00:51,045
You also had three rules for this file:

16
00:00:51,495 --> 00:00:54,483
change only what's between the quote marks,

17
00:00:54,933 --> 00:00:57,467
never touch a quote mark itself,

18
00:00:57,917 --> 00:00:59,314
and leave the commas alone.

19
00:01:00,214 --> 00:01:01,955
Today, you go a little further.

20
00:01:03,155 --> 00:01:04,615
At the top there's a note.

21
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:08,510
Then a named box, which is empty for now,

22
00:01:08,960 --> 00:01:12,871
and the word shared means every block in the file can see it.

23
00:01:13,771 --> 00:01:17,564
Next, a line that reads a crew roster, which is for Class 3.

24
00:01:18,464 --> 00:01:20,876
Then three lines that make your side,

25
00:01:21,326 --> 00:01:22,910
and one for the music.

26
00:01:23,810 --> 00:01:26,893
And here, at the left edge, is the map.

27
00:01:27,793 --> 00:01:31,345
This is a label, which means a named block,

28
00:01:31,795 --> 00:01:36,573
and everything indented under it runs once, when the game starts.

29
00:01:37,773 --> 00:01:42,271
Line thirty-five reads your whole fact sheet, and fills the box.

30
00:01:43,171 --> 00:01:46,823
After that, each section is handed to the thing that knows what to do with it:

31
00:01:47,273 --> 00:01:49,375
landmarks, quests, and scans.

32
00:01:50,276 --> 00:01:52,917
Now look at the word in quotes: landmarks.

33
00:01:53,817 --> 00:01:55,888
That's the key in your section heading.

34
00:01:56,788 --> 00:02:00,109
Last time, I said it had to be exactly that word,

35
00:02:00,559 --> 00:02:01,787
and this line is why.

36
00:02:03,587 --> 00:02:08,298
The lines for sides, for a cast, for conversations and for ruins

37
00:02:08,748 --> 00:02:11,709
do nothing until your file has those sections.

38
00:02:12,609 --> 00:02:15,283
Then comes the station, and then the hulk,

39
00:02:15,733 --> 00:02:19,633
where you added ghost ship to this line yourself, back in Lecture 7.

40
00:02:20,533 --> 00:02:23,931
And the last line is arrow, END,

41
00:02:24,381 --> 00:02:26,985
which says this block is finished.

42
00:02:28,185 --> 00:02:31,102
There are three things to know, and that's all the theory.

43
00:02:32,002 --> 00:02:33,388
The first is the indent:

44
00:02:33,838 --> 00:02:37,049
it's four spaces, and the lines of a block line up.

45
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:40,234
The second is arrow END:

46
00:02:40,684 --> 00:02:43,100
the block is done, and nothing under it runs.

47
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,659
And the third is these two blocks, which you already know.

48
00:02:48,559 --> 00:02:50,637
Each one ends by saying a name.

49
00:02:51,537 --> 00:02:53,641
This one says ghost ship found,

50
00:02:54,091 --> 00:02:56,344
which is your word, from Lecture 7.

51
00:02:58,144 --> 00:03:00,176
And the step in your fact sheet says,

52
00:03:00,626 --> 00:03:03,035
done when, signal, ghost ship found.

53
00:03:03,935 --> 00:03:06,632
So that step isn't finished by reach.

54
00:03:07,082 --> 00:03:09,528
It's finished by the script, by name.

55
00:03:10,428 --> 00:03:12,672
You'll paste that same line in a few minutes,

56
00:03:13,122 --> 00:03:15,178
and decide for yourself when it's said.

57
00:03:16,378 --> 00:03:18,079
Here's the server's start screen,

58
00:03:18,529 --> 00:03:22,574
which is what you get when you start the game without map equals zero.

59
00:03:23,474 --> 00:03:27,170
In its list of maps, mine is still called AMD Sample,

60
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:29,371
with the template's sentence under it.

61
00:03:30,271 --> 00:03:32,871
Your mission got a title in Lecture 3,

62
00:03:33,321 --> 00:03:35,327
but the map inside it never did.

63
00:03:36,227 --> 00:03:39,805
Both of those come from lines twenty-five and twenty-six.

64
00:03:40,705 --> 00:03:43,227
So change the words between the quotes.

65
00:03:44,127 --> 00:03:46,210
The line under it is the description,

66
00:03:46,660 --> 00:03:48,910
which is the sentence on that screen.

67
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:53,497
It has one quote mark, at the start, and none at the end,

68
00:03:53,947 --> 00:03:55,517
and that's how it's meant to be.

69
00:03:56,417 --> 00:03:57,926
Just keep it on one line.

70
00:03:58,826 --> 00:04:00,970
And there it is on the start screen,

71
00:04:01,420 --> 00:04:03,944
Salvage Run, with my own sentence under it.

72
00:04:05,144 --> 00:04:07,014
It's one command, as always.

73
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:11,074
Look at the last line: one AMD, and one mast.

74
00:04:11,974 --> 00:04:14,997
Lint has been reading the script every time,

75
00:04:15,448 --> 00:04:18,015
it's just never had anything to say.

76
00:04:19,815 --> 00:04:23,757
So now I break it, by taking out one quote mark.

77
00:04:24,657 --> 00:04:29,498
Lint says story dot mast, compile, line twenty-five,

78
00:04:29,948 --> 00:04:31,717
and it can't read that line.

79
00:04:32,617 --> 00:04:34,330
And its last sentence says

80
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:38,157
nothing in this mission runs until this is fixed.

81
00:04:39,057 --> 00:04:40,260
Here's the game with that file:

82
00:04:40,710 --> 00:04:44,460
a page headed Mast Compiler Errors, and nothing else.

83
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:46,926
Nothing of mine is running,

84
00:04:47,376 --> 00:04:48,904
and that's from one character.

85
00:04:49,804 --> 00:04:53,391
So, run lint after every change to this file.

86
00:04:54,591 --> 00:04:55,925
Now back to the story,

87
00:04:56,375 --> 00:04:58,769
which runs hulk, lifeboat, home.

88
00:04:59,669 --> 00:05:01,232
I want a wait before home,

89
00:05:01,682 --> 00:05:04,764
so the lifeboat step now reveals a new one.

90
00:05:05,664 --> 00:05:09,392
And the new step is done when it hears a signal, tug arrived,

91
00:05:09,842 --> 00:05:11,264
which is my own word.

92
00:05:12,164 --> 00:05:15,953
Lint says the tug step waits for the signal tug arrived,

93
00:05:16,403 --> 00:05:18,036
and nothing in the mission sends it.

94
00:05:18,936 --> 00:05:20,501
You've seen this warning before,

95
00:05:20,951 --> 00:05:22,887
and it's right, because nothing does yet.

96
00:05:24,087 --> 00:05:25,537
Go to the end of the file,

97
00:05:25,987 --> 00:05:27,066
and it's always the end.

98
00:05:27,966 --> 00:05:31,218
First a note, so I know what this is, and then the route.

99
00:05:32,118 --> 00:05:33,936
The game says quest started

100
00:05:34,386 --> 00:05:36,491
every time a hidden step is revealed,

101
00:05:36,941 --> 00:05:38,677
and this block listens for that.

102
00:05:39,577 --> 00:05:44,270
But it runs only if the step is this one, salvage, slash, tug,

103
00:05:44,720 --> 00:05:47,228
which is the address you write after reveal.

104
00:05:49,028 --> 00:05:50,164
Then there's one line,

105
00:05:50,614 --> 00:05:52,157
and you've read this line before,

106
00:05:52,607 --> 00:05:54,745
because it's how the hulk gets on the map.

107
00:05:55,645 --> 00:05:57,728
Here's what this one puts on Helm's map:

108
00:05:58,178 --> 00:06:00,908
the Salvage Tug, with her name beside her.

109
00:06:01,808 --> 00:06:04,012
The line says where, and that name,

110
00:06:04,462 --> 00:06:06,564
then its side and its role,

111
00:06:07,014 --> 00:06:08,633
and what it looks like.

112
00:06:09,533 --> 00:06:12,790
Those are the same facts as a landmark,

113
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:15,315
and the difference is when.

114
00:06:16,215 --> 00:06:18,375
And then arrow, END.

115
00:06:19,575 --> 00:06:22,328
Card two is the line from line ninety-three,

116
00:06:22,778 --> 00:06:25,209
with my word in it, tug arrived,

117
00:06:25,659 --> 00:06:28,145
and it's lined up with the line above.

118
00:06:29,045 --> 00:06:32,222
Lint is clean, because something sends the signal now.

119
00:06:34,022 --> 00:06:38,101
Card three is a wait, of twenty seconds.

120
00:06:39,001 --> 00:06:41,215
The lines run from the top down,

121
00:06:41,665 --> 00:06:45,111
so it waits, brings the tug in, and finishes the step.

122
00:06:46,011 --> 00:06:49,228
Then my word list gets a new role and a new signal,

123
00:06:49,678 --> 00:06:50,736
and lint is clean.

124
00:06:51,936 --> 00:06:53,557
Here are four mistakes.

125
00:06:54,457 --> 00:06:57,237
The first is one space short, on one line.

126
00:06:57,687 --> 00:07:00,993
Lint tells me: bad indentation, and the line.

127
00:07:01,893 --> 00:07:08,257
The second is a line pasted one line too low, under arrow END.

128
00:07:09,157 --> 00:07:10,427
It's a warning this time,

129
00:07:10,877 --> 00:07:13,653
and it says this line never runs.

130
00:07:14,553 --> 00:07:15,585
It's only a warning,

131
00:07:16,035 --> 00:07:17,465
but it would stop my story.

132
00:07:19,265 --> 00:07:22,290
The third is the card pasted in the middle of the map.

133
00:07:23,190 --> 00:07:24,291
It's the same warning,

134
00:07:24,741 --> 00:07:26,483
but about a line of the template,

135
00:07:26,933 --> 00:07:30,653
and the first thing it says is to move that line up.

136
00:07:31,553 --> 00:07:34,105
Don't do that, because that line is fine.

137
00:07:35,005 --> 00:07:36,946
My card cut the map in two,

138
00:07:37,396 --> 00:07:41,258
and the game would start with no station and no hulk.

139
00:07:42,158 --> 00:07:45,853
So move the card, to the end of the file.

140
00:07:47,653 --> 00:07:50,362
The fourth is the address, misspelled.

141
00:07:51,262 --> 00:07:54,450
Lint says clean, and there's no tug, ever.

142
00:07:55,350 --> 00:07:57,404
Nothing can check that word for you.

143
00:07:58,304 --> 00:08:00,913
The page has the list of what lint cannot see.

144
00:08:01,363 --> 00:08:03,275
It's short, so read it twice.

145
00:08:04,475 --> 00:08:07,624
Out to the hulk, and on to the lifeboat.

146
00:08:08,524 --> 00:08:12,377
Helm says Quest complete, Find the Lifeboat,

147
00:08:12,827 --> 00:08:15,422
and there's the new step in the Quest Log,

148
00:08:15,872 --> 00:08:19,092
but there's no tug on Helm's map, so now I wait.

149
00:08:20,892 --> 00:08:23,847
And there she is on the map, the Salvage Tug,

150
00:08:24,297 --> 00:08:26,351
with the name from my card beside her.

151
00:08:27,251 --> 00:08:31,398
Helm says Quest complete, Wait for the Tug,

152
00:08:31,848 --> 00:08:34,080
and in the Quest Log, home is revealed.

153
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:37,434
So it's back to the station,

154
00:08:37,884 --> 00:08:40,049
and there's my Win sentence on Game results.

155
00:08:40,949 --> 00:08:42,590
And both logs are empty.

156
00:08:43,790 --> 00:08:47,500
So that's three cards: when, finish a step, and wait.

157
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:50,794
For your turn, paste the first one again,

158
00:08:51,244 --> 00:08:53,010
change started to succeeded,

159
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:57,290
and make something of your own arrive when a step is finished.

160
00:08:58,190 --> 00:09:01,260
Next time is the capstone: you ship a mission.
